{
    "background_story": "Meadow was a lovable pig who lived on a small farm surrounded by rolling hills and green pastures. She loved nothing more than spending her days rooting around in the mud and oinking with delight. But Meadow had a secret passion - she was a master of the art of slow-cooked spareribs. Every summer, the farm would host a BBQ festival, and Meadow would sneak into the kitchen to watch the chefs at work. She'd sniff out the tenderest ribs and offer her expert opinion (a series of approving grunts). The chefs adored Meadow and would save her the best ribs, which she'd devour in happy silence. As the years passed, Meadow became the farm's unofficial sparerib connoisseur, and her love for the dish was legendary among the farmhands.",
